good news for Star Wars fans as ahsoka  tano will appear in the second season of  the Disney plus series the Mandalorian  according to Deadline actress rosario  Dawson has been signed for this role  the fans are of course excited even if  currently only a guest role as planned  actress rosario Dawson is known from the  Sin City movies and Marvel's daredevil  among others  her character ahsoka tano is known from  the animation series Star Wars the Clone  Wars a member of the intelligent people  of the Toccata and born on the planet  Chile  she began her training as a Jedi at the  age of three and after the outbreak of  the Clone Wars she was assigned to the  Jedi Knight Anakin Skywalker as a  Padawan the relationship between the two  is very difficult in the beginning but  develops over time into a close bond the  fact that rosario Dawson takes over the  role of ahsoka tano has met with  positive approval from fans so far the  second season of the Mandalorian is  scheduled to start this autumn but the  worldwide pandemic could put a damper on  the whole thing shortly after 2018  DC's Aquaman was released and a huge  success at the box office  it was obvious that there would be a  second part now the first details of the  plot are revealed as screenwriter David  Leslie Johnson mccottry answered some  fan questions on Twitter when asked if  there is a specific comic template for  the new movie the author answered that  Aquaman 2 is not based on a specific  story but has many elements of the  so-called Silver Age storyline with  Black Manta more precisely this means  that we can probably count on an intense  battle between Aquaman and Black Manta  apart from Jason Momoa the cast will  also include jaya abdullah teen as his  opponent Black Manta whether willem  dafoe  and Nicole Kidman will also play a role  in the second part is not yet clear this  cinema release of Aquaman 2 is scheduled  for December 16th in 2022 most people  know Angry Birds as a mobile game  classic or more recently as a movie the  only thing that's really missing is a  serious isn't it that's probably what  Rovio entertainment and cake thought  because together with Netflix they want  to produce their  own serious about the colorful pigs and  birds the serious is supposed to have  over 40 episodes each of them will be  about 11 minutes long the story revolves  around teenage versions of red bump and  Chuck who spent the summer together in a  camp the rival camp consists who would  have thought it of pigs therefore there  should be a fair amount of conflict  potential it is currently not known when  Netflix plans to release the series  after we already announced some  postponement of upcoming movies and  ongoing serious productions last week  there are more top-class movies and  serious since then that will do the same  and stop their production first of all  there is the Walking Dead series its  final episode where the title a certain  doom won't be broadcasted on US  television on April 12th as planned  therefore the release of the episode in  other countries will also be canceled a  new date for the release of episode 16  is not yet known but AMC announced that  the season finale will be released later  this year as a kind of special episode  this is more than understandable as The  Walking Dead team is currently already  having difficulties completing the  post-production of season 10  successfully on AMC's Twitter channel  the first photo from the final episode  was posted showing Norman Reedus  character Daryl Dixon standing among a  bunch of fighters for non-english  speaking countries the impact will also  be significant as the current situation  means that in most countries the latest  episodes cannot be synchronized at the  moment Warner Brothers and ICI have a  similar situation as their movie Wonder  Woman 1984 will not be able to keep its  actual release date either the parties  involved have decided to postpone the  film until August 14th for the time  being  previous on-demand release is probably  not relevant at the moment  director patty Jenkins explained the  reason for this on Twitter where she  said that Wonder Woman 1984 was made for  the big screen and that local cinema  owners would benefit from seeing the  blockbuster exclusively in the cinema  however many people think that the new  date for August is hard to maintain as  most people expect that the world  cinemas who won't open their doors again  by mid-august however there are good  news from China where things are slow  but surely returning to normal in many  parts of the country and while the last  cinemas around the world are closing  China is in the process of opening them  since the worldwide film industry is at  a standstill at the moment and no new  movies are being produced they decided  to simply show some classics on screen  among them are some Avengers movies and  James Cameron's Avatar bizarrely enough  avatar could now regain the first place  of the most successful movies of all  times because the difference in the  income of the two movies is only a  ridiculous 9 million u.s. dollars this  amount could be brought into the cinemas  by the huge Chinese film industry in a  few days assuming that of course more  people want to see Avatar than the  parallel running Avengers endgame which  most journalists assume regarding the  more than 10 years ago release date of  course we will keep you up to date on  all the consequences of the virus on the  movie industry in the coming weeks  [Music]
 

